  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A single-tier cotton plant hanger holds one pot. The standard 10, 15 cm terracotta or plastic pot that sits on a windowsill. The cup is worked in double crochet in the round from a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "magic ring",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", then the hanging cords extend upward and gather at the top loop. DK cotton gives a clean, non-stretchy cup that holds the pot weight without distorting."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The cup is worked flat in the round to a diameter that fits around the base of your chosen pot. The four hanging cords are then crocheted up from the cup rim and joined at a gathered loop 40, 50 cm above. Total cotton: roughly 80 m of DK cotton."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "slug": "crochet-hook",
              "label": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "isOptional": false
            },
            {
              "slug": "tapestry-needle",
              "label": "Tapestry needle",
              "isOptional": false
            },
            {
              "slug": "craft-scissors",
              "label": "Scissors",
              "isOptional": false
            },
            {
              "slug": "stitch-marker",
              "label": "2 stitch markers",
              "isOptional": false
            },
            {
              "slug": "measuring-tape-soft",
              "label": "Soft measuring tape",
              "isOptional": false
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Materials"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "80 m DK cotton (100% cotton or cotton-linen blend). One ball of 100 m DK cotton is enough for one hanger with off-cuts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "1 small metal ring, 2, 3 cm diameter, for the hanging loop (a curtain ring works well)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "16 dc × 20 rows = 10 × 10 cm in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook, unblocked. Gauge is not critical for plant hangers. The cup size adjusts by changing chain count. Work a quick swatch and see how your fabric drapes; a looser tension suits this project."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring (MR)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st). UK and US"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Double crochet (dc). UK; this is single crochet (sc) in US terminology"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr). UK; this is double crochet (dc) in US terminology"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cup base"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "magic ring",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Work all rounds in a continuous spiral: place a stitch marker on the first stitch of each round and move it up as you work."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 1: 6 dc into the magic ring (6 sts)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: 2 dc in each st (12 sts)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 3: *1 dc in next st, 2 dc in next st; repeat from * around (18 sts)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 4: *1 dc in each of next 2 sts, 2 dc in next st; repeat from * around (24 sts)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 5: *1 dc in each of next 3 sts, 2 dc in next st; repeat from * around (30 sts)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 6: *1 dc in each of next 4 sts, 2 dc in next st; repeat from * around (36 sts)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 7: *1 dc in each of next 5 sts, 2 dc in next st; repeat from * around (42 sts)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Check that the base fits under your pot. The base should be slightly smaller than the base of the pot. The cup walls will grip the pot. For a 10 cm pot, rounds 1, 5 (30 sts) are usually enough. For a 13 cm pot, rounds 1, 6 (36 sts). For a 15 cm pot, work rounds 1, 7 (42 sts)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cup sides"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "From the last base round, work straight (no increases) for 4 rounds of dc. This creates the cup wall that holds the pot. Close the final round with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "slip stitch",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "slip-stitch"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " into the first st, ch 1, turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hanging cords (work 4)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Divide the cup rim into 4 equal sections. Mark the quarter points with stitch markers. On each marked section, work a hanging cord as follows:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Join yarn at the first marker with a sl st."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Ch 3 (counts as first tr), work 2 tr into the next 2 sts at the marker point (3 tr total)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Turn. Ch 3 (counts as first tr), 2 tr into the top of the previous tr group."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Repeat step 3 for a total of 13 rows (or until the cord measures 40 cm from the cup rim). Each group of 3 tr makes the cord body."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fasten off, leaving a 30 cm tail for gathering."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gather and hang"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Thread the 4 tail ends through the small metal ring."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pull all 4 tails even and tie a square knot directly against the ring."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Trim to 2 cm below the knot and weave the ends back through the cord with the tapestry needle."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in the starting tail from the magic ring tightly. Give the cup a light steam with a steam iron held 5 cm above the fabric. This tightens the cotton and firms up the cup shape. Do not press the iron down onto the crochet."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Handwash in cool water with a drop of washing-up liquid. Rinse and squeeze gently. Do not wring. Hang to dry naturally. Cotton plant hangers can go in a 30°C machine wash on a gentle cycle if needed; reshape while damp."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "problem": "The cup is too loose and the pot tips",
              "cause": "Too many base rounds. The cup diameter is larger than the pot base",
              "fix": "Undo back to where the diameter matched the pot base and redo the cup sides from there"
            },
            {
              "problem": "The hanging cords twist around each other",
              "cause": "The cords are not evenly spaced around the cup rim: one quarter-point was off",
              "fix": "Recount the stitches between each cord to ensure 4 equal sections, then reattach any misplaced cord"
            },
            {
              "problem": "The metal ring slips back through the gathered cords",
              "cause": "The tails were not knotted tightly enough against the ring",
              "fix": "Tie a second square knot over the first, or add a small length of yarn wrapped tightly around all 4 cords below the ring"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}